---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site';

---

<PageLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  description={`Learn what information ${SITE.name} collects, why it is used, how it is protected and what privacy choices are available to you.`}
  lede="What we collect, why we collect it, and how to tell us to stop."
  updated="October 12, 2026"
>
  <p>
    This policy explains how {SITE.name} ("we", "us") handles information when you visit
    <strong>{SITE.url}</strong>. We have tried to write it in plain language. If anything is
    unclear, email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> and we will explain.
  </p>

  <h2>Information we collect</h2>
  <p>We keep this deliberately minimal. There is no account system and no login on this site.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Information you give us.</strong> If you email us, we receive your email address and
      whatever you write. The contact form opens your own email application; it does not submit
      information to this website.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Technical data.</strong> Our hosting provider may process server requests and technical
      information needed to deliver the pages. We do not currently offer an account or newsletter signup.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Browser storage and advertising technologies.</strong> Saved ideas are stored in your
      browser. Google advertising code may use cookies, web beacons, IP addresses, or other identifiers
      as described below.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not collect payment details, government identifiers, or health information, and we do not
    knowingly collect information from children under 13.
  </p>

  <h2>How we use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To publish and improve the site, and to understand which articles are useful.</li>
    <li>To reply to messages you send us.</li>
    <li>To provide the saved-ideas feature in your browser.</li>
    <li>To display advertising if ad serving is enabled.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Advertising and Google AdSense</h2>
  <p>
    Google AdSense code is present on this site. If ads are served, Google and other third parties
    may place and read cookies on your browser or use web beacons and IP addresses to collect
    information as a result of ad serving. This may be used to deliver and measure ads, subject to
    your available choices and applicable consent requirements. Learn more about
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can opt out of personalised advertising by visiting
    <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Google Ads Settings</a>,
    or opt out of third-party vendor cookies at
    <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">aboutads.info</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Consent in the EEA, UK and Switzerland</h2>
  <p>
    A Google-certified consent management platform has been published in our AdSense account for
    visitors in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom, and Switzerland. It provides
    choices for advertising data use where applicable. If you do not see an expected choice or
    need help changing one, contact us at the address below.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>We do not sell your personal information. We share data only with:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Google AdSense</strong> — advertising delivery and measurement.</li>
    <li><strong>Our hosting provider</strong> — to serve the site.</li>
    <li><strong>Legal authorities</strong> — where we are legally required to.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct, export or delete the
    personal information we hold about you, and to object to certain processing. Residents of the
    EEA and UK have these rights under the GDPR; California residents have comparable rights under
    the CCPA/CPRA, including the right not to be discriminated against for exercising them.
  </p>
  <p>
    To make a request, email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. We will
    respond within 30 days.
  </p>

  <h2>Retention and security</h2>
  <p>
    We keep email messages for as long as needed to handle the conversation. The site is served over HTTPS. No method of transmission
    over the internet is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We will update this page when our practices change, and we will move the "last updated" date at
    the top. Material changes will be noted on the homepage.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about this policy: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
  </p>

</PageLayout>
